The problem is that in your while condition you have
while (choice != "left" || choice != "right")
But if choice is "left", then choice != "right" is true, so the whole condition is true. So the loop will run forever. You need to use && instead of ||.
But even better, you can check if the choice is not one of the allowed options. So:
while (!choice.equals("left") && !choice.equals("right"))
So the loop continues as long as the choice is not left and not right. Once the choice is either, the loop exits.
Also, when comparing Strings in Java, you should use equals(), not == or !=.
